with reasoning. So we need to respond as James Carter in Round 2, building on that.\n\nWe have our own notes. We should consider candidate C strengths and concerns. We might want to ask for more info about Candidate C's stress resilience and technical competence, as per shared mental model. But we can also give our own perspective. The instruction: If we need info, we should use tool calls before public message. We have missing info: stress resilience (calm in crisis) for C is known: \"C keeps calm in a crisis\" from our notes. Also \"C understands complicated technology\". So we have that. So we can incorporate those facts.\n\nWe should evaluate other candidates maybe. But we need to respond to Sarah's recommendation. We can either agree, or challenge, or add nuance. Provide evidence: C is reliable, quick decisions, positive crew atmosphere, calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. We can argue that communication difficulty may affect crew cooperation, but positive crew atmosphere suggests overall cooperation is okay. Egocentric may be mitigated by leadership qualities? Not sure.\n\nWe could also bring up other candidates as alternatives, but we need to compare. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate B also handles stress well, conscientious, good weather assessment, but makes nasty remarks about colleagues, which is a serious crew cooperation issue. Candidate A has leadership but is a show-off and not open to new ideas, which may affect adaptability. Candidate D solves problems well, takes responsibility, but has hot temper and know-it-all attitude, which may affect crew cooperation.\n\nThus we can support Candidate C as best overall.\n\nWe need to produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\".\n\nLet's craft a concise public message: \"I agree with Sarah's provisional recommendation of Candidate C. The candidate's 100% reliability, quick correct decisions, calmness in crisis, and strong technical understanding meet the core criteria. While there are concerns about communication and egocentric attitude, the positive crew atmosphere suggests these are manageable. Compared with other candidates, B's interpersonal issues and A's lack of openness, D's hot temper, make C the strongest overall fit.\"\n\nYes.\n\nProceed."}
